{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113000-dimsci-resources","id":1113000,"title":"DimSci Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-07T17:13:29-07:00","id":1113000,"title":"DimSci Resources","content":"I'm wondering if anyone has any good (VE) Diemsional Science resources. I have a few from a MUSH I was on years ago, but looking back at them they seem less than sufficient for a good PDC campaign.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T02:56:08-07:00","id":1113165,"title":"","content":"Have you got the revised ve convention book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:17:33-07:00","id":1113209,"title":"","content":"Yes I do. Love the book, but I'm looking for Everett Volume-type stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:23:37-07:00","id":1113213,"title":"","content":"The VE Convention books are the only place which really talk about the umbra from the Technocratic point of view. Outside of those I can only recommend Infinite Tapestry and Book of Worlds, and you'll just have to adapt what they give you into a VE paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:31:55-07:00","id":1113217,"title":"","content":"No, I know there aren't many Mage books that talk about it, but I was thinking additional resources to help spark some ideas. Novels, games, etc. that might discuss 'getting from the dimension to the one three over.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T11:39:54-07:00","id":1113301,"title":"","content":"Ooh, alright then:<br /> All of star trek <br /> Sliders <br /> Fringe <br /> Alan Moore's swamp thing (when he's in space) - in fact, 2000AD, marvel, dc and a lot of other comics do multi-dimension stuff<br /> And despite being a big fan of military science fiction, I can't actually think of anything else that fits. Parallel worlds are not common in the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:41:41-07:00","id":1113326,"title":"","content":"Star Trek is only slightly less limited than VE Rev when it comes to things like Everett Volumes. I thought of Sliders (duh), but it doesn't have the engineering technobabble I'm looking for, iirc.<br /> <br /> Fringe, though. Hmm. I'll have to check it out. Thanks. :^)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:37:13-07:00","id":1113384,"title":"","content":"Books:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Madeleine L'Engle's A Wrinkle in Time<br /> John C. Cramer's Einstein's Bridge<br /> Michael Crichton's Timeline<br /> Carl Sagan's Contact</div>Movies:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Event Horizon (1997)<br /> Deja Vu (2006)<br /> Interstellar (2014)<br /> Cube 2: Hybercube (2002)</div>Video Games:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mass Effect series</div>RPGs:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Trinity: Stellar Frontiers</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:00:50-07:00","id":1113402,"title":"","content":"I'll second Event Horizon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T19:20:09-07:00","id":1113498,"title":"","content":"Comics: Planetary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T00:26:48-07:00","id":1113635,"title":"","content":"Sons of ether revised also has a rote for visiting llel universes, and I'm pretty sure the void engineer version would be similar. The intro story is a etherite version of a trip to an Everett volume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:40:01-07:00","id":1113747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113000-dimsci-resources?p=1113498#post1113498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comics: Planetary</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're on the subject of comics: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Science_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Black Science</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:50:15-07:00","id":1113754,"title":"","content":"I wrote an entire post with other suggestions, but the lack of an &quot;undo&quot; key and an errant key stroke ate the whole thing.<br /> <br /> I guess I'd add the way the current Flash TV show handles Earth-2, 14, S, etc. by having a machine in the basement they can and do use when they aren't mucking with some very confusing time travel issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:04:29-07:00","id":1113760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113000-dimsci-resources?p=1113635#post1113635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sons of ether revised also has a rote for visiting llel universes, and I'm pretty sure the void engineer version would be similar. The intro story is a etherite version of a trip to an Everett volume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good, but they would definitely need to be re-tasked for a VE game. The VE aren't brave explorers into the unknown in the same way. They are more &quot;Go interesting places, Meet interesting people and Kill them&quot; types. Even if the players are brave and bold and senstive and interested, that's not their bosses or their mission statement. They are the soldiers on the walls of reality keeping the Masses safe from the Dark Things Outside The World They Know. They are the modern incarnation of the Age of Exploration, sure, but that comes with all the baggage of imperialism, colonialism, assimilation and ethno/genocidal tendencies. <br /> <br /> For example, the ones that deal with the Dark Umbra don't want to understand it and what it means about death and souls and the like. They want to stop ghosts from haunting people (and reinforce the Union's view on what those things should mean... which will continue to raise the Shroud and, in turn, keep people from being haunted). <br /> <br /> They don't want to open the expanded universe up for exploration. They've already GOT that version of the spirit worlds pinned down. It's Conventional Space (except for the BEM version of EDE's and they are dealing with that, right behind that Threat Null boondoggle). They want to make those other places go away, or, at least be as distant as possible. If that's not possible (which it probably isn't), they want to control access and keep them on the downlow. <br /> <br /> Like I said, the mileage may vary for the players and their characters. The sidelined part of the VE's that deal with the hidden places of the world and 'our next door neighbors (because, ya know, it's not SPACE) might very well recruit dewey-eyed, climb-the-mountain-because-it's-there types, but there are going to be some issues along the line when the bosses swoop in and go for locking the door and throwing away the key on Cool Place X or figuring out how to exploit it for the &quot;public good&quot;. And those are likely to be the best possible options.... (Wait a sec..Why were their battle-hardened space marines on deck to go through the Gate to the place with the cure and friendly squirrel people?)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:04:50-07:00","id":1113838,"title":"","content":"I always sort of viewed the Void Engineers as these people who started, way way back in the day (like, the Bronze Age) as something similar to Dreamspeakers and as the centuries went by, went from sort of &quot;keepers of the gates to the other worlds&quot; to being more focused on understanding and controlling what was on the other side, to being extremely afraid of it and being obsessed with keeping it away from Earth and humanity. They're like the people who show up at Eliot's house in the last act of &quot;E.T&quot;., except that their end game includes the firebombing plan from &quot;Outbreak&quot;, because they really and truly believe that it'll turn into &quot;The Strain&quot; if they don't. <br /> <br /> But then my take on the Technocracy as a whole has kind of diverged from printed material, not least of which in that I found ways to give all five Conventions ancient foundations, two in Rome, one in Greece, one in Egypt and one (the VE) in Canaan. So I am weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:24:12-07:00","id":1113895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113000-dimsci-resources?p=1113838#post1113838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always sort of viewed the Void Engineers as these people who started, way way back in the day (like, the Bronze Age) as something similar to Dreamspeakers and as the centuries went by, went from sort of &quot;keepers of the gates to the other worlds&quot; to being more focused on understanding and controlling what was on the other side, to being extremely afraid of it and being obsessed with keeping it away from Earth and humanity. They're like the people who show up at Eliot's house in the last act of &quot;E.T&quot;., except that their end game includes the firebombing plan from &quot;Outbreak&quot;, because they really and truly believe that it'll turn into &quot;The Strain&quot; if they don't.<br /> <br /> But then my take on the Technocracy as a whole has kind of diverged from printed material, not least of which in that I found ways to give all five Conventions ancient foundations, two in Rome, one in Greece, one in Egypt and one (the VE) in Canaan. So I am weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I buy the bits about what the VEs are like now a la Peter Coyote in ET with some fuel air bomb action, though I would probably lay some of that at the feet of the N.W.O. The VE's would probably be like the bad guys in Stranger Things. &quot;Here's a weird gate. Let's put a guy in a space suit through it. Oh yeah, maybe a probe or two first?&quot; (So.... add Stranger Things to the list but that's just one other dimension. And the obvious one should be Stargate, just take out &quot;planet&quot; for &quot;go through gate to different world&quot;).<br /> <br /> Professionally as an archaeologist, I don't really buy continuity from the Bronze Age for pretty much at all. Anywhere. Anything. Except for, say, some very rare solid material remnants that typically don't mean now what they meant then. (A rare exception would be something like the foundations of the stone walls between the fields in Cornwall, many of which do date to the Bronze Age). Anything else is wishful thinking and/or propaganda. The VE's were derived from the Explorators (who were definitely way worse in the imperialism aspects, but probably more open to goofy, Etherite-type experiences as well). We really don't have much in the way of belief systems or anything else around, and, on the rare occasions we do, there is 4000 years or so of massively skewed interpretation. Those guys were in derived from the combination of the Celestial Masters and the Void Explorers, but, let's face it, the division between the two is pretty much there and the Celestial Master side ended up on top in a big way with the addition of less &quot;thinking about stuff in our towers&quot; and more fieldwork. <br /> <br /> Before that, whatever the antedents were, they don't have that much to do with the VEs as they are now. When any Convention starts claiming &quot;Oh, Mohenjo Daro? That was us....&quot; or &quot;The first time people walked out of their valley just to see what was out there (which would be <i>Homo erectus</i> about 1.5 mya at the latest), that was the beginning of us&quot;, they should get a swift kick in the pants from anyone who is allowing that statement for anything other than it's propaganda value","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:17:13-07:00","id":1113927,"title":"","content":"Somewhat unrealistic levels of continuity are a staple of the conspiracy theory/secret society genre. Probably because they're sometimes fun to play with.<br /> <br /> But, in my own WoD, each of the five go back a ways (and the SoE and VA were never part of the Technocracy, save for those who defected to them later). My - and I stress the word &quot;my&quot; - Void Engineers start as the Openers of Ways, a cult devoted to the sacred wisdom of Kothar-wa-Khasis as keepers of the gates to the underworlds and other realms, as well as sailers, navigators and astrologers, and were most active among the Phoenicians. By the time of the Christianization of the Roman Empire, they'd mostly fallen into obscurity. But by the late Middle Ages, a number of people who were trained in some of their secrets and traditions form the Celestial Masters, who seek to harness the secrets and powers of the heavens for their own ends as diviners, explorers and philosophers. By the time of the formation of the Enlightened Society of Technocratic Reason in the 19th century, they're the Watchers of the Void, believing that threats lie &quot;out there&quot;. And after WW2, they're fully the Void Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T10:57:30-07:00","id":1114210,"title":"","content":"I get it. I did that sort of game once as well, but on a HUGE scale with the characters are lineal resurrections of ancient mages of note that traced the origins of mage groups all the way back to Egypt, with little stops along the way like having some of the original mages gathered together by Bonisagus to create the Order of Hermes as prior incarnations, followed by their being scattered among the founders of both the Order of Reason and the Traditions. It can be fun, but it's just achingly implausible and, in the &quot;typical&quot; run of things seems like something rationalists in the Union would be dead set against. Especially if the objective is the control the message, the narrative is pretty much &quot;We, the present, aimed at the future, are GREAT and those old guys had it wrong&quot;. Appeals to authority should be less about &quot;this is what someone who I have little connection did a long time ago&quot; and more with &quot;look what I am doing NOW and this, this, this and THIS are what I'm doing next...) The Union is pretty much as futurist as they come. <br /> <br /> Kothar is pretty much a smith god with a sideline in palace building (when an appropriate commission comes directly from El) and the odd bow (when he's seduced or threatened or both into it... then she gives it away to her latest moral boy toy...). Why is he messing around with gates and other worlds and such? Seems more like a Wepwawet kinda thing (up to and including Opener-of-Ways is actually an epithet of his) and/or Min (if you can get around the somewhat graphic iconography...), or, really, Ptah, since any attribution of Opener to Kothar's name is a late thing that seems like it has to do with conflation or syncretism with Ptah (who is another explicit Opener). Melkart was more an explicit Canaanite/Phoenician god of traveler and is linked with Tyre and the spread of the Phoenicians across the Mediterranean and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T15:56:34-07:00","id":1114303,"title":"","content":"To be honest, It's been so long since I worked all that out I can't remember where my source material came from. IIRC, the idea came from something I read about Kothar being credited with inventing both boats and navigation (I think he's one of those gods like Isis and Ptah who get credited with inventing everything), as well as being involved in divination, mixed with the fact that I wanted my proto-VE to be attached to Carthage and the Phoenicians. And by the time you get to Carthage, there's so much cultural mix and matching going on with everyone that's it almost maddening for the amateur mythologist to figure out what goes where and when. I do recall that I picked the name &quot;Openers of the Ways&quot; because I thought it sounded cool. (Same reason I picked Architects of the Monolith for the Egyptian proto-Iteration X and the Order of Aesclepius for the Grecian Apollo cult that were the seeds of the Progenitors.) And like I said, it's not an unbroken evolution for any of them. My (somewhat loose and flexible according to what I need it for) timeline has the Openers more or less having died out as an actual organized group before the fall of the western Roman empire, with only a few master-student relationships to pass on their lore, and a totally new group, the Celestial Masters, arising just ahead of the Age of Exploration. Likewise, the Architects of the Monolith are all but gone by the time the Roman Masters of the Rule show up, and they're pretty much gone (outside of parts of the Byzantine empire) when the Craftmasons are formed, and so on with the International Brotherhood of Mechanistics and Iteration X. <br /> <br /> But, in regards to it's level of implausibility, [shrug], this is a game with space ships battling over the moons of Jupiter, trinary computers and Terminators roaming the streets. So I figure plausibility is a matter of taste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:26:41-07:00","id":1114345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113000-dimsci-resources?p=1114303#post1114303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, It's been so long since I worked all that out I can't remember where my source material came from. IIRC, the idea came from something I read about Kothar being credited with inventing both boats and navigation (I think he's one of those gods like Isis and Ptah who get credited with inventing everything), as well as being involved in divination, mixed with the fact that I wanted my proto-VE to be attached to Carthage and the Phoenicians. And by the time you get to Carthage, there's so much cultural mix and matching going on with everyone that's it almost maddening for the amateur mythologist to figure out what goes where and when. I do recall that I picked the name &quot;Openers of the Ways&quot; because I thought it sounded cool. (Same reason I picked Architects of the Monolith for the Egyptian proto-Iteration X and the Order of Aesclepius for the Grecian Apollo cult that were the seeds of the Progenitors.) And like I said, it's not an unbroken evolution for any of them. My (somewhat loose and flexible according to what I need it for) timeline has the Openers more or less having died out as an actual organized group before the fall of the western Roman empire, with only a few master-student relationships to pass on their lore, and a totally new group, the Celestial Masters, arising just ahead of the Age of Exploration. Likewise, the Architects of the Monolith are all but gone by the time the Roman Masters of the Rule show up, and they're pretty much gone (outside of parts of the Byzantine empire) when the Craftmasons are formed, and so on with the International Brotherhood of Mechanistics and Iteration X.<br /> <br /> But, in regards to it's level of implausibility, [shrug], this is a game with space ships battling over the moons of Jupiter, trinary computers and Terminators roaming the streets. So I figure plausibility is a matter of taste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very particular sort of Union game that can hew that way. It's effectively going to end up with ultimate revelations bending to the Traditions being on the right side of history. (OMG the Rosicrucians are right!) The universe really is elephants (e.g. ancient conspiracies of culturally collaberative mages) all the way down.... The Union is sorta purpose built to be futurist and the modern VE's even more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:13:42-07:00","id":1114838,"title":"","content":"Well, no. In 1st edition, they were pretty clearly made out to be monsters. While this was toned down a bit in second edition, the Technocracy as an RPG antagonist faction was always originally conceived as being about Control, not Science. It's why they are named after a real world sociopolitical philosophy. But because a number of early WW writers were NeoRomantics, there was always a bad tendency for anything generally on the late-Baby Boomer/Gen X list of things considered &quot;bad&quot; to be laid at the feat of Pentex/the Wyrm, the Technocracy, Banality or which ever Vampire clan was out of fashion that month, while anything on the &quot;good&quot; list was claimed for that writer's favorite splat. Often, this included the entire Industrial Revolution as &quot;bad&quot;. In Mage, this only really changed when Jess Heinig, who IIRC had a degree in cybernetics, became Developer and a champion of the Union as a viable alternate focus for the game. <br /> <br /> From a personal standpoint, I think this was a mistake (and I largely feel the same way about the Sabbat in Vampire). The Technocracy are the monsters of the modern age, the experts, elites and faceless bureaucrats of the 20th century who've given us the Communist murder machines, the failed inner cities, the Vietnam war, America's public school system, the eugenics movement, the level of public service at the DMV, Prohibition, the War on Drugs, the FCC, video game rating systems, &quot;fake but accurate&quot; as a standard of journalism, Watergate, Waco, the Great Depression, the Tuskegee syphilis experiments, forced sterilization, utilitarian medical ethics, and at least a hundred other things. But this was never going to happen, as the majority of WW's staff and fandom have always leaned left of center, and dealing with the above would require admitting that technocratic statism is as much a beloved idea of the progressive left as it is of the modern day inheritors of the Whigs on the right. <br /> <br /> I believe that the real futurists of Mage are the Sons of Ether, who remember that science (or rather Science!) is as much about wonder and discovery as it is about discipline and rules. <br /> <br /> As for the concept of &quot;consensual reality&quot;, I quite frankly hate it. It has always made it nigh impossible for people to actually discuss the game; Any discussion becomes the equivalent of trying to talk about the idea of humans going back to the moon with a NASA engineer, a bureaucrat who only cares about the price tag, a community activist decrying it as a waste of money, a conspiracy theorist who insists the Apollo missions were faked, another conspiracy theorist who insists that the government is hiding the existence of FTL technology, and a stoner who insists that the moon is made of green cheese. It is absolutely maddening. <br /> <br /> In my games, reality is what it is, but there's the Tapestry underlying it as a metaphysical framework, and being one of the Awakened means that you can fiddle with the Tapestry to make changes in reality. But the bigger the changes - and the more unbelievable they are to unawakened bystanders - the more the Tapestry is going to resist, and may at some point even actively fight back with the Scourge. In my WoD, the Technocracy want to guide and control humanity into what the elites of the Union believe they should be; the Traditions want people to be free to find their own path to enlightenment. And as part of that, the Sons of Ether's Ethernautical Society are explorers, while the Void Engineers are sanitizers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:12:41-07:00","id":1115081,"title":"","content":"Since the real world philosophy involved is about the rule of scientists, I guess it's about Control, but only inasmuch as ANY idea of governing other people is about... well... &quot;Control&quot;. It's the science part that distinguishes the Technocracy, from, say, the Celesital Chorus's predecessors and their Islamic counterparts who were also about &quot;Control&quot; in the Middle Ages, but with different slant on how that Control was supposed to work. Long and short, what makes the Technocracy the Technocracy isn't a focus on Control, it's the science part. Lots of different groups of folks are and have been all about Control per Control but they aren't coming at it from the same direction as the Union.<br /> <br /> The Union as a whole (which is something that can be said about them... there isn't really any such thing as &quot;the Etherites as a whole&quot;) is much more solidly futurist per the classic constituent elements of that philosophy than the Etherites are. And much more grounded in science. Etherite science is about Eureka moments and personal discovery. In fact, SCIENCE! is really about discovery per se and not as much about implementation. Etherites are more often than not individualists and some of them aren't really even vaguely scientific (if you're a pulp adventurer who won that toss of the genetic dice and learns your psychic powers from theosophist-like Hidden Masters, you can definitely be an Etherite, they even have a specific group for those folks, but they aren't even close to being &quot;scientists&quot; as per the common meaning of that term, much less what the Technocrats are doing). If you're science is more about wonder and discovery than about rules and discipline, it's not really as much about science and, more specifically, engineering, particularly in the sense that a lot of what they are doing is intended to be rolled out to the Masses in accordance with the Time Line.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers are both sanitizers and explorers. Humans explore. That's one of those human things. The Union doesn't actively suppress that; it's enabling it. If it did suppress , there wouldn't be a Convention of explorers which is descended from other groups focusing on exploration. It's just trying to constrain that exploration in such a way that the exploration doesn't open humanity as whole up to being endangered and exploited by external entities. Conventional Space is Human Space, but that doesn't mean it is pre-mapped with each and every bit already known as if it was created wholesale according to some model. Just because they don't want squishy things with tentacles to be eating people doesn't mean they aren't out there mapping the unknown. They don't explore in the same way that the Etherites do (anymore than they do in the same way the VA's do, or the Dreamspeakers for that matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}